FinShield AI does not use “tickets” in the support-desk sense. It uses **fraud alerts** and **investigation cases**.

Case and alert features (docs/PRD.md):
- **Fraud alerts:** Created by ML, rules, watchlist match, or manual; workflow: Open → Investigating → Escalated → Resolved (Confirmed Fraud / False Positive) / Dismissed. Assignment, bulk actions, escalation, resolution notes.
- **Cases:** Created from one or more alerts (or manually); link alerts, transactions, entities, evidence. Workflow: Open → In Progress → Pending Review → Escalated → Closed (Confirmed Fraud / False Positive). Timeline, assignment, findings.
- **Automation:** Auto-assignment rules, notification on severity (email, SMS, in-app), webhook on alert/case events. SLA-style metrics (resolution time, confirmed fraud rate) for reporting.

Rules:
- Alerts and cases are first-class entities in the data model (docs/DB_SCHEMA.md); link to transactions, entities, rules, models.
- Workflow and assignment logic in services, not in route handlers; support async (e.g. Celery) for notifications and report generation.
- Audit trail for status changes, assignments, and resolutions.
- Idempotency and clear audit trail for automated actions (e.g. webhook triggers).

Do not:
- Put alert/case creation or assignment logic only in HTTP handlers; support Event Hub and batch flows.
- Trigger notifications or webhooks without retry and audit.
